<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Jafrabad State</h1><p class="st-meta">1650 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Jafrabad</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Kathiawar port held as a dependency by the Siddi Nawabs of Janjira, far down the western coast.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Jafrabad was a port on the southern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Kathiawar</a>. It later passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siddis">Siddis</a> of Janjira, the African-descended naval chiefs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konkan-coast">Konkan coast</a>, who kept it as a distant dependency.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Nawab of Janjira ruled Jafrabad through a local governor, and its income came from fishing, coastal trade and customs. The British treated it as part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/janjira-state">Janjira State</a>, though it lay geographically in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Kathiawar</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Together with Janjira, Jafrabad acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and was merged in 1948. It became part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> in 1960 and is a fishing port in Amreli district.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/jafrabad-state.jpg" alt="Jafrabad State" width="320" height="160"><figcaption>Image: This vector image was created by Ali Zifan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jafarabad_State_Merchant_Flag_vector.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1650 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Jafrabad</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Islam, Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gujarati</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Jafrabad</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1799&amp;focus=jafrabad-state" aria-label="Jafrabad State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6600 1406 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Jafrabad State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6920 1662L6979 1755M6920 1662L7364 1602M6920 1662L6896 1610"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6979 1755h0M7364 1602h0M6896 1610h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6920 1662h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6920 1662h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1799&amp;focus=jafrabad-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
